    "result_text": "The only remaining references are in the acceptance test itself (its comment and its assertion that the old fields are gone) \u2014 which is expected and passing. \n\nThe implementation is complete. Here's a summary of what I did to unify `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId`:\n\n## Changes\n\n**New: `MemberIdGenerator`** (service) \u2014 builds the unified id `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`:\n- `REGION` \u2014 region code from postcode/city\n- `FY` \u2014 2-digit fiscal year of the registration date (via existing `FiscalYear`)\n- `HASH8` \u2014 the same first-8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName` (via existing `Sha256Hex`)\n- `CHK` \u2014 a single Luhn digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>` (via existing `LuhnCheckDigit`)\n\nIt reuses the existing model utilities rather than duplicating any algorithm.\n\n**Removed** the now-obsolete `CustomerCodeGenerator` and `MembershipNumberGenerator`.\n\n**`Owner`** \u2014 dropped the `customerCode` (`customer_code`), `membershipNumber` (`membership_number`) fields, the derived `getCheckDigit()`, and the `getPrimaryIdentifier()` indirection (its purpose \u2014 surviving this unification \u2014 is now fulfilled). Added `memberId` (`member_id`). `getLocality()` now resolves the region directly from postcode/city via `LocalityResolver` (same result the memberId's `REGION` segment is built from), instead of parsing it out of the old dash-separated code.\n\n**`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`** \u2014 generates a single `memberId` (passing the registration date for FY) in one block; collision handling now applies to `memberId` (`deduplicateMemberId`).\n\n**Audit** \u2014 `OwnerAuditLogger` and `OwnerCreatedEvent` now reference `memberId` (the JSON event field is renamed `memberId`).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema properties with `memberId`; updated the `locality` description.\n\n**DB schemas** (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres) \u2014 replaced `customer_code` + `membership_number` columns with a single `member_id`.\n\nThe full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`). The audit output confirms the format, e.g. `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (NSW + FY 27 + HASH8 `16E6609E` + check digit `1`).",
